{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/423588-abyssal-headless-horsemen","id":423588,"title":"Abyssal Headless Horsemen","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-28T17:28:07-08:00","id":423588,"title":"Abyssal Headless Horsemen","content":"So, there are a number of us who are sure that someone who has JUST been decapitated has the time to accept the Black Exaltation, especially given the frozen moment of time in which the deal is offered.<br /> <br /> But can Abyssal Exalted support being a headless horseman in an effective manner? Or rather, while it's cool for the Exalt that he survived, his head is still off, and that can be extremely inconvenient in lots of ways.<br /> <br /> Playing such an inconvenienced character would be fine for a flaw, I suppose. Though it's a rather big flaw, to always need one arm free (or a specialized sling) for carrying your own head around, not to mention what can happen if you find yourself disarmed of your head.<br /> <br /> To advance beyond this concept as a flaw, there are at least three possible routes.<br /> <br /> 1) You reattach your head, either in the immediate rush following the Final Breath, or later through magical medicine. However, this is no good for someone who wants to play a &quot;headless&quot; Abyssal.<br /> <br /> 2) You transfer the seat of your consciousness into your body, complete with the ability to see and hear without eyes or ears. Call this the &quot;Celty Sterluson / Dullahan&quot; route. This way, you don't really need your head except to talk, though it works like a lich's phylactery in that destroying it would kill you. You might also suffer memory loss or something from being separated from it for too long.<br /> <br /> 3) You learn how to make your head levitate and fly around on its own power. Call this the &quot;Sekibani / Nukekubi&quot; route. It's even compatible with reattaching your head, since your head can fly around on its own, it makes no difference if it lands on your neck.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T17:54:14-08:00","id":423632,"title":"","content":"I took the first option, back when I made Son of Void Dragon, an Abyssal based in part off of Vlad Dracula (and with a touch of Hellsing's Alucard, naturally).<br /> <br /> Materials suggested for Liminals seems to suggest that they can survive decapitation, or even anything short of having their brains destroyed, though I doubt a Liminal's gonna go doing option 3; he'll probably need someone to sew him together a new body (a la the Limper from <i>The Silver Spike</i>.<br /> <br /> That said, I wouldn't shoot down a Dullahan Abyssal if the player absolutely wanted it, though it's far from my preferred style of play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T19:10:45-08:00","id":423680,"title":"","content":"You carry your head around like a proper dullahan, complete with bone chariot, spine whip and a bucket of blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T22:31:16-08:00","id":423853,"title":"","content":"I'd allow someone to add a stunt to Malicious Parody Imposter to use your own head as the replacement. Not sure if it can do much that Face Drinking Bite and some other social charms can do but <i>it's cool.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T22:40:11-08:00","id":423857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/423588-abyssal-headless-horsemen?p=423680#post423680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You carry your head around like a proper dullahan, complete with bone chariot, spine whip and a bucket of blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>By bone chariot, you mean awesome motorcycle, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T02:54:01-08:00","id":423931,"title":"","content":"This question is dependent upon a metaphysical question regarding how the exaltation affects the body/mind/soul paradox. Existing Liminal information suggests that the brain is the seat of exaltation, not the heart, and if the black exaltation worked the same way then the still sentient part of you would be the free-floating head. In which case there are any number of ways to play an abyssal as a head that is carried/flying/in a jar or whatever as a person. Of course if you wanted to you could play it the other way (the Celty case is particularly unusual in that it is suggested by the material that her body and head, after prolonged separation might very well be two different people in some sense), but the mechanics of Exalted don't really allow an exalt to see without eyes in the manner of a dullahan though.<br /> <br /> Part of the issue with this concept is that, from a standard mechanics perspective you have created a situation in which it is difficult to adjudicate how the character can be killed. If you exist as a free-floating head but can acquire a body and still use all your Abyssal charms but do not die when the body dies then that's actually a massive advantage, not a flaw (and probably poaching on Liminal territory). Such a concept probably works best for games that aren't going to stress dice-based outcomes very much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1j0RQNTrhSQVIjBJw3555qA1S9Hih1SRwychiPhEwm9k/pub\" target=\"_blank\">Whitescrub Tundra Project</a>: a fan-made setting reference for Exalted 3e.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10769032/1/\" target=\"_blank\">Edge of Underleaves</a> A pair of dragon-blooded dare the jungles of the southwest.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4060-mechalich","name":"Mechalich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4060_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T08:36:29-08:00","id":424180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/423588-abyssal-headless-horsemen?p=423931#post423931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This question is dependent upon a metaphysical question regarding how the exaltation affects the body/mind/soul paradox. Existing Liminal information suggests that the brain is the seat of exaltation, not the heart</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it suggests that the brain is vital to LIMINAL Exaltation. Which doesn't need to apply to anyone else, because no one else has the inherent ability to come back from the dead so long as their brain is intact.<br /> <br /> Other Exalted might be able to cheat death through other organs.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, even if in the Celty option I mentioned making your body the seat of your consciousness, I also said that destroying your head would still kill you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T08:50:18-08:00","id":424193,"title":"","content":"FWIW, the artbook for the Limited Edition core in 1e had a deathknight who had apparently done just this--his head seemed to float a little above his stump.<br /> <br /> That said, I'd be inclined to go with a variant of #2: The head is gone. Your dude is running around without a head forevermore, and while it may function as an arcane link in the short term, it may either immediately rot away upon death, or just do so naturally rather than being a long-term secret weakness, because that's something more akin to the Deathlords than the Deathknights. The Deathknight may have charms to work around their inability to talk, but sensory abilities generally work just fine.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T09:14:42-08:00","id":424205,"title":"","content":"My inclination would be to treat headlessness as just a rad variation of the Mute flaw.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/423588-abyssal-headless-horsemen?p=423857#post423857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By bone chariot, you mean awesome motorcycle, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun fact: Celty was the inspiration for all of Abyssal Drive that I wrote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}